//! The version-chain machinery: every family is one chain of per-version structs from its
//! floor version to the newest, plus a beta struct; each struct parses the JSON as written in
//! its era and a typed `Upgrade` step carries it forward. Public in this crate so
//! `bedrock_addon`'s content modules can implement it; hidden at the facade.
//!
//! - [`Family`] describes a family: payload key, floor, range model, beta permission, the
//!   component table and its hooks; [`VersionChain`] is its chain, generated by
//!   [`version_chain!`](crate::version_chain) over [`VersionStruct`]s linked by [`Upgrade`].
//! - [`load`] is the whole pipeline of one file: envelope, version selection, parse (with the
//!   Molang pass 1), upgrade to the newest struct, generic and family validation.
//! - [`RangeModel`] turns a chain's versions into version ranges; [`select`] picks a struct.
//! - [`parse_component_map`], [`parse_component`] and [`validate_components`] are the
//!   per-component halves: one component at a time from its slice, and the
//!   `released` / `requires` / deprecation / `supersedes` / area checks on the newest struct.
//! - [`testing`] reads a family's step file (`<family>.toml`) and checks each `Upgrade` impl
//!   against its ops.

